                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Too much like other rpg maker games with sprites, sound effects, combat and beyond. Nothing really unique to distinguish the game from any other rpg.",
                        "timestamp_created": 1791460020,
                        "timestamp_updated": 1791460020,
                        "voted_up": false,
                        "votes_up": 0,
                        "votes_funny": 0,
                        "weighted_vote_score": 0.5,
                        "comment_count": 0,
                        "steam_purchase": true,
                        "received_for_free": false,
                        "written_during_early_access": false,
                        "developer_response": "To follow up on this - you're right. I originally made this game to come out before I graduated with a degree in Game Design as something of a portfolio buffer, specifically to highlight the ideas I had as it relates to RPG systems and turn based battle mechanics. On the whole, as a one person team who compiled all the resources and developed the 30+ hour player experience by myself, I am both proud of what I accomplished here and accepting of exactly this criticism. \n\nAll of this went into consideration when taking the price tag away from the base game and just letting people try it if they wanted absolutely free - and I thank you for giving it the chance you did!\n\n//bryan",
